PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL
FOR SETTLEMENT PURPOSES ONLY

SETTLEMENT OFFER OF TRANSWESTERN PIPELINE COMPANY
 DOCKET NOS. RP97-288-009, ET AL
SEPTEMBER 30, 2001


  Transwestern Pipeline Company (“Transwestern”) has carefully considered the various concerns and issues raised by the Commission in its several orders issued in this proceeding, and by the Commission Staff and the parties in prefiled testimony and on brief.  Transwestern is of the view that these concerns and issues could be addressed by negotiated modifications to Transwestern’s current FERC Gas Tariff and its capacity award procedures and posting formats.  Accordingly, Transwestern proposes the following settlement principles, which are designed to be implemented by specific tariff language that will be drafted as part of the settlement process. 


Transwestern Capacity Postings

Transwestern will post short term capacity  (i.e., less than five months) for a minimum term of two business days
Transwestern will use interactive open season procedures for all operational capacity transactions
Transwestern will incorporate all aspects of its capacity posting procedures in specific tariff language
Transwestern will post the specific bid evaluation methodology as part of every capacity posting.
Transwestern will use pro rata allocation  unless Transwestern specifically identifies an alternative methodology
Transwestern will work in good faith to simplify the exising posting formats on its electronic bulletin board
 

Awarding of Capacity

Transwestern will remove capacity award language from the “right of first refusal” and “capacity release” sections of its tariff and will incorporate all aspects of its capacity award procedures in a section of the tariff specifically designated for that purpose 
Transwestern’s new capacity award tariff language will set out one mandatory set of requirements and processes to be followed for all capacity award situations and will eliminate certain discretion present in Transwestern’s current procedures


Transwestern is developing tariff language to implement the above proposals and will provide it to Staff upon completion.  

If Transwestern and Staff can reach conceptual agreement as discussed above, Transwestern and Staff will jointly attempt to achieve a unanimous settlement.  

The proposal outlined above is contingent on (1) agreement on acceptable tariff language to implement the concepts discussed, (2) completion of an unanimous offer of settlement to be filed in the referenced proceeding, and (3) Transwestern’s management approval.

  


  
 
